# Rerun scripts: `cd` first

When the user asks to rerun a script (e.g. "rerun `X`", "run it again", "rerun minsarApp..."), always:
1. `cd` into the project directory first (the repo root where `minsar/` lives).
2. Then execute the command.

Rationale: several MinSAR bash launchers use `pwd` to decide where logs/jobfiles are written (e.g. `WORKDIR=$(pwd)`), so the working directory matters.

